A. THE DAVENPORT-HEILBRONN KAPPA DIAL
==============================================================================
Gauss sum tau            = (-1.17557050458495 + 1.90211303259031j)   |tau|^2 = 5.0
root number eps          = (0.85065080835204 + 0.525731112119134j)   arg eps = 31.7174744115 deg
kappa_+ = tan(arg eps/2) = 0.28407904384041229603
kappa_DH (closed form)   = 0.28407904384041229603   |diff| = 1.97e-31
kappa_- = -1/kappa_+     = -3.5201470213402019924   (the antisymmetric functional equation)
(1+i k)/(1-i k) = eps at kappa_+ and = -eps at kappa_-  [checked to 1e-25]

A2. Functional-equation test  |Lam(s) - Lam(1-s)| (even) and |Lam(s) + Lam(1-s)| (odd)
  kappa_+ : even-defect   2.96e-31   odd-defect       1.52
  kappa_- : even-defect       1.28   odd-defect   7.86e-31
  kappa=0 : even-defect     0.0954   odd-defect       1.41
  kappa=1 : even-defect       0.24   odd-defect        1.8
  kappa = +i gives L(s,chi) exactly, kappa = -i gives L(s,chi-bar) exactly  [checked]
  involution kappa -> -1/kappa: fixes +-i, swaps kappa_+ <-> kappa_-  [algebra: (1-ik)L+(1+ik)Lbar -> difference combination]

