A4. Mirror orbit at the certified off-line zero (f_kappa_+ has real coefficients + functional equation)
  |f(s0         )| =   9.84e-15    |L(chi)| = 0.70219735   |L(chi-bar)| = 0.70219735
  |f(conj s0    )| =   9.84e-15    |L(chi)| = 0.70219735   |L(chi-bar)| = 0.70219735
  |f(1 - s0     )| =   3.62e-14    |L(chi)| = 2.5834945   |L(chi-bar)| = 2.5834945
  |f(1 - conj s0)| =   3.62e-14    |L(chi)| = 2.5834945   |L(chi-bar)| = 2.5834945
  -> at a zero of f the two constituents have EQUAL modulus and opposite matched phase; neither vanishes.

