==============================================================================
C. PLANE-COLOURING ARITHMETIC
==============================================================================
C1. Rotation angles 2 arcsin(1/(2R)) move a point at distance R by exactly 1: cos = 1 - 1/(2R^2)
  R^2 = 3  (Moser spindle):  cos = 5/6  = 0.833333333333, e^(i theta) = (5 + sqrt(-11))/6
  R^2 = 4  (de Grey):        cos = 7/8  = 0.875000000000, e^(i theta) = (7 + sqrt(-15))/8
  R^2 = 16 (de Grey):        cos = 31/32= 0.968750000000, e^(i theta) = (31 + 3 sqrt(-7))/32
  identities checked to 1e-12:
    (5+sqrt-11)/6  = -conj(alpha/alpha-bar),  alpha = (1+sqrt-11)/2, norm 3   [3 splits in Q(sqrt-11)]
    (7+sqrt-15)/8  = -conj(beta/beta-bar),    beta  = (1+sqrt-15)/2, norm 4   [(beta) = p^2, p above 2 in Q(sqrt-15)]
    (31+3sqrt-7)/32= -(gamma/gamma-bar)^4,    gamma = (1+sqrt-7)/2,  norm 2   [2 splits in Q(sqrt-7)]
  i.e. each rotation is, up to a half-turn (a lattice symmetry) and a mirror, the angle pi/pi-bar of an ideal of norm R^2.

C2. The hexagonal 7-colouring is Z[omega] mod (3 + omega), an ideal of norm 7
  Eisenstein norms that occur: [0, 1, 3, 4, 7, 9, 12, 13, 16, 19, 21, 25] ...  (5 and 6 do NOT occur: 2 is inert)
  minimal squared lattice distance between same-coloured centres = 7  (= N(3+omega))
  admissible hexagon circumradius r in (0.3872, 0.5000): diameter 2r < 1 and same-colour tiles >= sqrt(21) r - 2r > 1
  e.g. r = 0.45: diameter 0.90 < 1, same-colour separation >= 1.1622 > 1  -> a valid 7-colouring
  a norm-N Eisenstein ideal works iff sqrt(3N) > 4, i.e. N > 5.333: N = 7 is the first norm that occurs -> 7 colours
  square tiles on Z[i]: need N > 8; Gaussian norms [0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 9, 10, 13, 16] -> N = 9 = 3^2 (3 inert): 9 colours, the classical square-grid count
  lattice unit-distance graphs themselves: Z[i] mod (1+i) -> 2 colours; Z[omega] mod (1-omega) -> 3 colours.

